  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "How to read this view",
      "items": [
        "Each row is an independent guarded transition, not a chronological sequence across rows. Repeated phase labels name the same underlying phase; aliases prevent unrelated rules from sharing ambiguous drawing corridors. The normal-procedure view supplies the connected happy path."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "Reading this view",
      "items": [
        "snake_case labels are real session.phase strings. 'established + granted' is phase 'established' with session.granted = True (carrier.py 856). Nodes tagged conceptual or 'phase group' are not phase strings.",
        "Pilot pattern calls advance only with a radar track and range checks (_pattern 1222-1252). touchdown and on_deck come from mission telemetry, and on_deck is debounced (overlord_carrier.lua 563-576)."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "rose",
      "title": "Rules",
      "items": [
        "A land contact is not a trap. Leaving the deck after contact is a bolter (carrier.py 55-56). A pilot's bolter call counts only while the track shows the aircraft airborne (1285-1293).",
        "When an enrolled aircraft touches down or traps, every other session in 'ball' is waved off for a foul deck (702-706). Calling the ball on a foul deck waves the caller off (1243-1244).",
        "A granted recycle keeps the lane and session.granted. Ungranted contacts go back to holding (680-686).",
        "_foul_deck blocks new grants while any session is in touchdown or on_deck (803-805, 866)."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "slate",
      "title": "Transition evidence (file lines)",
      "items": [
        "bolter, granted CASE I/II: airborne after contact, CASE I/II (638-639, 690-691)",
        "bolter, granted CASE III: CASE III recycle (687-689)",
        "bolter without lane: ungranted contact (680-686)",
        "wave off: pilot call or foul deck (1280-1283, 702-706); CASE III CASE III recycle (1280-1283)"
      ]
    }
  ]
